cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "zf-approx: zero forcing approximation via nice path decompositions"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-24"
authors:
  - family-names: Cameron
    given-names: Ben
  - family-names: Janssen
    given-names: Jeannette
  - family-names: Mathew
    given-names: Rogers
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Zhiyuan
repository-code: "https://github.com/OwenZZY/CJMZ_ZF"
url: "https://github.com/OwenZZY/CJMZ_ZF"
abstract: >-
  A standard-library-only Python implementation of the deterministic approximation
  algorithm for the zero forcing number. Given a graph and a path decomposition of
  width w, it returns a zero forcing set S, a fort packing F and the forcing arcs A
  with |S| <= (w+1)|F|.
keywords:
  - zero forcing
  - fort packing
  - path decomposition
  - approximation algorithm
